course: dictionary
lesson: 15684
title: Timekeeping: time, clocks and being on time
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Timekeeping is a word about time, but it can mean three things: being on time, measuring time, or how well a clock keeps the right time. The words around it are its context, and they show you which meaning fits. «Her timekeeping has improved, so she is never late now.» The clue is late, so timekeeping here means being on time.
explain: «The timekeeper stopped the race when the last runner crossed the line.» The clue is race. A timekeeper measures the time, so timekeeping here means measuring and recording time. «The old clock had poor timekeeping and ran five minutes slow.» The clue is ran slow, so timekeeping means how well the clock keeps the right time.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. Does «her being on time has improved» still make sense? Yes, so you have found the right meaning.
fact: Timekeeping means being on time, measuring time, or how well a clock keeps the right time.
fact: A timekeeper measures and records time, for example in a race or a match.
fact: Sundials, clocks and calendars are all tools that people have used for timekeeping.
fact: In maths, timekeeping problems use a start time, an end time and the duration between them.
fact: Timekeeping is uncountable, so we say «good timekeeping», not «a timekeeping».
exercise: «Her timekeeping has improved, and she is never late now.» What does timekeeping mean here? | Keeping a pet safe | Measuring time in a race | How well a clock keeps time | *Being on time
exercise: «The timekeeper stopped the race when the last runner crossed the line.» What does a timekeeper do? | Sells tickets | Fixes broken clocks | Runs the race | *Measures and records time
exercise: Which of these is a tool used for timekeeping? | Umbrella | Football | Pencil case | *Calendar
test: «The old clock had poor timekeeping and ran five minutes slow.» What does poor timekeeping mean here? | The clock was too big to move | The clock was painted badly | The clock made a loud noise | *The clock did not keep the right time
test: In a maths problem the start time is 3 o'clock and the end time is 5 o'clock. What do you need to find? | The name of the timekeeper | *The duration between the times | A sundial | The colour of the clock
exam: Which phrase is an example of good timekeeping? | Missing the bus every day | Forgetting your lunch | Losing your pencil case | *Arriving at school on time
